oculus first and then I went over to HTC  vive so there was something I didn't  notice that you stood out a little bit  more for you going the opposite  direction and that's the field of view  is a little bit limited the field of  view is it limited on the oculus rift  compared to the current model of the HTC  vive that said the vibe does have more  of a screen door effect when you notice  individual pixels on the displays and  that is one thing that takes you out of  immersion in quote-unquote as much as we  can really say that now as does the  field of view with the oculus so both of  them have their shortcomings at the  moment I will say each device is way  more comfortable than they have been in  the past showings the vibe in particular  it's lighter in general but it also has  sort of a dual strap thing going on and  back your head feels really light I  didn't actually notice that I was  wearing anything bulky having a light  headset something that's comfortable is  gonna be really really important one  thing that's a problem for both of them  though is this cave  that's sticking out no matter what  they're gonna have to have something  that tethers it to the PC in one of our  demos we had a person who was just  walking around behind us and making sure  we didn't trip over it but that's what  are you gonna do and that's in your home  that's something you really have to  solve for that is another problem they  have to solve and there are a lot of  problems and then again one of them  being software which we talked about you  know recently as well and while it's  fair to say that any of the demos on  these these platforms could have been  used in either headset these companies  are showing specific demos and so we can  really only say what they have based on  what they've shown us and the stuff I've  seen on vibe is much more consistent and  impressive at this point eval Curie has  always been the standout demo on oculus  but when I was doing things today in the 